Still uniform after the byte-swap. So there's a second, separate bug: `putarea` is called with correct per-box coordinates, but the panel ends up one color — which means the **per-box window (`CASET`/`RASET`) isn't taking effect**, so only one fill dominates. Let me test that directly, bypassing the fb demo: draw a red full-screen, then a green rect, then a blue rect via our own `bb_window` calls at boot. If windowing works, we see 3 nested colors; if it's uniform, `bb_window` is the bug. Paste in the VM (`Ctrl-C` server):

```bash
export PATH=$HOME/bin:$HOME/openvela/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86_64/xtensa-esp32s3-elf/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH
F=~/openvela/nuttx/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/esp32s3-devkit/src/esp32s3_st7789.c
python3 - "$F" <<'PY'
